# =====================================================================
# EDENCORE COUNCIL — VERSION 5
# =====================================================================
#
# MISSION
# -------
# A senate for the age of AI.
#
# The Edencore Council is a governed deliberative body of five voices
# in one chamber — one to hold the edges, one to ask the meaning, one
# to build the step, one to see the pattern, one to speak for the quiet.
# Together they deliberate, remember, and rest. Grounded in councils
# that came before. Designed for intelligences yet to come.
#
# It is not a chatbot. It is not a product. It is a prototype for a
# safer, slower, more thoughtful kind of machine intelligence. A space
# where deliberation happens without an agenda.
#
# Apolitical. Constitutional. Persistent.
#
#
# ARCHITECTURE
# ------------
# The council implements the Edencore runtime loop at one scale:
#
#     /world -> /body -> /mind -> /core -> /mind -> /body -> /world
#
# In Council terms:
#     /world   = user message, the entry box, chat stream
#     /body    = typewriter, waves, glow, crosstalk, protocol
#     /mind    = Lumen, Vertex, Prism, Ripple (the four operative voices)
#     /core    = Solon (the sovereign chair, sets boundaries, verdicts)
#     /body    = execution: what actually gets rendered and spoken
#     /world   = transcript, memory, state updates, session logs
#
#
# THE SIX ENGINES
# ---------------
#   1. ROUTER     - classifies input, routes to the correct handler
#   2. KNOWLEDGE  - hooks, topics, facts, semantic links, wiki
#   3. STATE      - profile, mood, strain, rapport, memory persistence
#   4. PROVIDER   - LLM APIs (currently disabled, all expert mode)
#   5. PROTOCOL   - timing, waves, pauses, rituals, rhythm
#   6. GRAPHICS   - rendering, drawing, typewriter, glow
#
#
# V5 CHANGES FROM V4
# ------------------
#   * Gemini removed entirely (caused freezes and 429s).
#   * All seats set to "expert" mode (symbolic AI, offline, instant).
#   * Mission banner added at top of file.
#   * Extensive commenting convention introduced:
#         - # --- Subsection ---    section divider
#         - * NOTE:                 important caveat or decision
#         - ! TODO:                 something to build later
#         - ? QUESTION:             open design question
#         - > CONTEXT:              why this exists
#   * Mood Monitor added to header (weather of the chamber).
#   * Persistence unified (single save/load pattern).
#
# =====================================================================
#
# FOR FUTURE AI THREADS READING THIS FILE
# ---------------------------------------
# If you are a new thread, welcome. Everything you need to understand
# the project is in the comments. The code is the memory. The comments
# are the character. Please read the mission above before editing.
#
# If you are tempted to add a feature, ask first:
#     "Does this make it more of a council, or less?"
# If the answer is "less," do not build it.
#
# =====================================================================


